––– comment –––
Shared bulk_import commit and error semantics: a commit while another data request is
active is refused and keeps the pool; an invalid document fails the pool for everybody until
a commit reports and removes it; a broken request body drops only its own unwritten tail; a
shared_join request never creates a pool.
––– block: ../base/start-searchd –––
––– input –––
cat > /tmp/shared.sh <<'EOF'
gen() { for ((i=$2; i<=$3; i++)); do printf '{"insert":{"table":"%s","id":%d,"doc":{"title":"doc %d","gid":%d}}}\n' "$1" "$i" "$i" "$((i % 7))"; done; }
post() { curl -sS -X POST "http://localhost:9308/bulk?bulk_import=$1&shared$2" -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' --data-binary @"$3" -w ' HTTP %{http_code}\n'; }
slow() { curl -sS --limit-rate "$3" -X POST "http://localhost:9308/bulk?bulk_import=$1&shared" -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' $4 --data-binary @"$2" -w ' HTTP %{http_code}\n' > /tmp/slow.reply 2>&1 & echo $! > /tmp/slow.pid; }
commit() { printf '\n' > /tmp/commit.ndjson; post "$1" "$2" /tmp/commit.ndjson; }
sql() { mysql -h0 -P9306 --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -e "$1"; }
leftovers() { echo "staging=$(ls /var/lib/manticore/$1 | grep -c indexer-rt-bulk) children=$(ps -eo args | grep -c '[i]ndexer_rt_bulk_chunk')"; }
EOF
––– output –––
––– comment –––
Busy: a slow data request (about 6 s for 2000 documents) is admitted before its body is read,
so a commit sent meanwhile gets 409 shared_busy and the pool stays open. After the slow
request is staged the commit publishes both requests.
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "CREATE TABLE s_busy (title TEXT, gid INT)"; gen s_busy 1 100 > /tmp/b1.ndjson; gen s_busy 101 2100 > /tmp/b2.ndjson; post s_busy '' /tmp/b1.ndjson
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":100,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; slow s_busy /tmp/b2.ndjson 20k; sleep 1; commit s_busy ''
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":1,"errors":true,"error":"shared bulk_import into table 's_busy' has other active requests","error_code":"shared_busy","shared_state":"busy"} HTTP 409
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; while kill -0 $(cat /tmp/slow.pid) 2>/dev/null; do sleep 0.2; done; cat /tmp/slow.reply; commit s_busy ''; sql "SELECT COUNT(*), SUM(id) FROM s_busy"
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":2000,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"published"} HTTP 200
2100	2206050
––– comment –––
Invalid document: the request that sent it gets 400, the pool keeps the first error and later
requests get 409 with that text; its children are killed and the table is released at once. The
commit returns the error with 500 and removes the failed pool and its staging files.
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "CREATE TABLE s_fail (title TEXT, gid INT)"; gen s_fail 1 100 > /tmp/f1.ndjson; printf '%s\n' '{"insert":{"table":"s_fail","id":101,"doc":{"title":"bad","nosuch":1}}}' > /tmp/f2.ndjson; post s_fail '' /tmp/f1.ndjson; post s_fail '' /tmp/f2.ndjson; post s_fail '' /tmp/f1.ndjson
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":100,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":1,"errors":true,"error":"unknown column: 'nosuch'","error_code":"shared_failed","shared_state":"failed"} HTTP 400
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":1,"errors":true,"error":"unknown column: 'nosuch'","error_code":"shared_failed","shared_state":"failed"} HTTP 409
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; commit s_fail ''; commit s_fail ''
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":1,"errors":true,"error":"unknown column: 'nosuch'","error_code":"shared_failed","shared_state":"failed"} HTTP 500
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":1,"errors":true,"error":"no shared bulk_import into table 's_fail' to commit","error_code":"shared_no_pool","shared_state":"no_pool"} HTTP 409
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; leftovers s_fail; sql "INSERT INTO s_fail (id, title, gid) VALUES (1, 'direct insert', 0); SELECT COUNT(*) FROM s_fail"
––– output –––
staging=0 children=0
1
––– comment –––
Ids are converted as by an ordinary insert: "12abc" is 12, " 7" is 7, "-5" is 2^64-5 and an
overflow is 2^64-1, where the indexer read the raw string and lost the row of "abc", "-5" or an
overflow without an error. A missing id or one that converts to 0 ("abc", "0") gets an auto-id;
an id error of an ordinary insert fails the pool like an invalid document.
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "CREATE TABLE s_ids (title TEXT, gid INT)"; printf '%s\n' '{"insert":{"table":"s_ids","doc":{"id":-5,"title":"negative"}}}' > /tmp/i1.ndjson; post s_ids '' /tmp/i1.ndjson | grep -o '"error":"[^"]*"\|HTTP [0-9]*' | tr '\n' ' '; commit s_ids '' | grep -o 'HTTP [0-9]*'; printf '%s\n' '{"id":"12abc","title":"tail","gid":1}' '{"id":" 7","title":"space","gid":2}' '{"id":"-5","title":"minus string","gid":3}' '{"id":"18446744073709551616","title":"overflow","gid":4}' '{"id":"52","title":"digits","gid":5}' '{"id":"abc","title":"letters","gid":6}' '{"id":"0","title":"zero string","gid":7}' '{"title":"no id","gid":8}' > /tmp/i2.ndjson; post s_ids '' /tmp/i2.ndjson; commit s_ids ''; sql "SELECT id, title FROM s_ids WHERE gid<=5 ORDER BY gid ASC; SELECT title FROM s_ids WHERE gid>5 AND id!=0 ORDER BY gid ASC"
––– output –––
"error":"Negative document ids are not allowed" HTTP 400 HTTP 500
{"items":[],"current_line":8,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"published"} HTTP 200
12	tail
7	space
-5	minus string
-1	overflow
52	digits
letters
zero string
no id
––– comment –––
Broken body: a request is killed after a few KB, less than one 32 KiB batch. Its tail is
dropped, the pool and its children stay, the next request is staged and the commit publishes
exactly the data of the complete requests.
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "CREATE TABLE s_break (title TEXT, gid INT)"; gen s_break 1 100 > /tmp/k1.ndjson; gen s_break 101 3100 > /tmp/k2.ndjson; gen s_break 3101 3200 > /tmp/k3.ndjson; post s_break '' /tmp/k1.ndjson
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":100,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; slow s_break /tmp/k2.ndjson 4k; sleep 2; kill $(cat /tmp/slow.pid); sleep 0.5; echo "children=$(ps -eo args | grep -c '[i]ndexer_rt_bulk_chunk')"
––– output –––
children=1
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; post s_break '' /tmp/k3.ndjson; commit s_break ''; sql "SELECT COUNT(*), MIN(id), MAX(id), SUM(id) FROM s_break; SELECT COUNT(*) FROM s_break WHERE id>100 AND id<=3100"
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":100,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"published"} HTTP 200
200	1	3200	320100
0
––– comment –––
The same with a chunked body, as the Fluent Bit plugin sends it: a connection lost before the
last chunk fails only that request, not the pool.
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "CREATE TABLE s_break_chunked (title TEXT, gid INT)"; gen s_break_chunked 1 100 > /tmp/c1.ndjson; gen s_break_chunked 101 3100 > /tmp/c2.ndjson; gen s_break_chunked 3101 3200 > /tmp/c3.ndjson; post s_break_chunked '' /tmp/c1.ndjson; slow s_break_chunked /tmp/c2.ndjson 4k '-H Transfer-Encoding:chunked'; sleep 2; kill $(cat /tmp/slow.pid); sleep 0.5; post s_break_chunked '' /tmp/c3.ndjson; commit s_break_chunked ''; sql "SELECT COUNT(*), SUM(id) FROM s_break_chunked"
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":100,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
{"items":[],"current_line":100,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"published"} HTTP 200
200	320100
––– comment –––
A pool that never received a batch (the only data request broke before 32 KiB) still commits:
its empty slot is closed without a build, the reply is published, no chunk is added and nothing
is left behind.
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "CREATE TABLE s_nothing (title TEXT, gid INT)"; gen s_nothing 1 3000 > /tmp/n1.ndjson; slow s_nothing /tmp/n1.ndjson 4k; sleep 2; kill $(cat /tmp/slow.pid); sleep 0.5; commit s_nothing ''
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"published"} HTTP 200
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM s_nothing; SHOW TABLE s_nothing STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'"; leftovers s_nothing
––– output –––
0
disk_chunks	0
staging=0 children=0
––– comment –––
A request with shared_join only joins an open pool: without one it answers no_pool and creates
nothing, as the commit after it shows; with an open pool it is staged like any other request.
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "CREATE TABLE s_join (title TEXT, gid INT)"; gen s_join 1 3000 > /tmp/j1.ndjson; gen s_join 3001 6000 > /tmp/j2.ndjson; post s_join '&shared_join' /tmp/j1.ndjson; commit s_join ''; post s_join '' /tmp/j1.ndjson; post s_join '&shared_join' /tmp/j2.ndjson; commit s_join ''; sql "SELECT COUNT(*), SUM(id) FROM s_join"
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":1,"errors":true,"error":"no shared bulk_import into table 's_join' to join","error_code":"shared_no_pool","shared_state":"no_pool"} HTTP 409
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":1,"errors":true,"error":"no shared bulk_import into table 's_join' to commit","error_code":"shared_no_pool","shared_state":"no_pool"} HTTP 409
{"items":[],"current_line":3000,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
{"items":[],"current_line":3000,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"published"} HTTP 200
